# Build output.
/target

# Coverage instrumentation. `cargo llvm-cov` writes raw profiles beside the
# build and an lcov report wherever it is pointed; none of it is reproducible
# input, so none of it belongs in the repository.
*.profraw
*.profdata
/lcov.info
/coverage
/target/llvm-cov
/target/llvm-cov-target
/target/nextest

# Generated SBOMs. `cargo cyclonedx` writes one file per workspace member,
# beside that member's Cargo.toml — it has no --output flag, so these land in
# the source tree whether or not that is wanted. They are release artefacts,
# built in CI and attached to the release: a committed SBOM changes on every
# dependency bump, conflicts on every Dependabot merge, and is wrong the moment
# nobody regenerates it.
*.cdx.json
*.cdx.xml
/bom.json
/bom.xml

# Mutation testing output. `cargo mutants` writes a full build and test log per
# mutant; the summary is what matters and CI publishes it as an artifact.
/mutants.out
/mutants.out.old

# Profiling and debugging output.
perf.data
perf.data.old
flamegraph.svg
*.heaptrack.*

# Editors. These are personal choices about how to read the code, not facts
# about the project, so they stay out of shared history.
/.vscode
/.idea
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
\#*\#
.\#*

# Operating systems.
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local environment overrides.
/.env
/.env.local
